Z||000000||Rodney||06-27-2001||10:52 PM||||I will soon be offering the A/C - engine strut shock bracket in steel. On the 3.4 there is one boss missing and what is the popular compromise is to weld a bolt in the hole where the boss is missing on the engine block. This makes it a spring board design with a cast iron piece not designed for that much stress. So I am replicating the bracket in cold rolled steel. I can't say I've heard of any failures but I would not be comfortable with the modified cast iron bracket. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||06-27-2001||10:54 PM||||Sweet.  I wasn't too comfortible with it either but I didn't have any other choice.  I will definitely buy one from you when you make it availible, while I am at it I will pick up a leather shift boot.||||reg||14
